# Exclusions of the mutation gate for the crate lauf (gates.sh, gate mutants, reads every mutants/*.liste).
# Format and rules: mutants/README.md. One entry per line: <list> <kind> <pattern>.

# lauf, `lauf-attrappe`: the stand-in of the tests (search process, model path, harness probe). The binary has
# `required-features = ["pruefbau"]`, so no delivery build compiles it (cargo build, also --release, skips it
# without the feature; no build script of the delivery switches the feature on), and it is never shipped. Its mutants
# test a test help, not the delivered program.
testhilfe datei crates/lauf/src/bin/attrappe.rs

# lauf, the modules of the same binary `lauf-attrappe`.
testhilfe datei crates/lauf/src/bin/attrappe/**

# lauf, `einthreadig`: each test case runs in a thread of libtest, so the run without the feature has no case with one
# thread; only the test build puts in the way that counts the threads. Caught in the run with the feature pruefbau.
erster re crates/lauf/src/kind.rs:148:5: replace einthreadig -> bool with false

# lauf, `lesen_text`: the delivered build reads no configuration from the test path (`cfg!(feature = "pruefbau")` comes
# first in the condition). Caught in the run with the feature pruefbau and by `tests/naht.rs`.
erster re crates/lauf/src/konfig.rs:174:76: replace == with != in lesen_text

# lauf, `bwrap_halten`: it is reached only once a real enclosure profile is built and the real `bwrap` holds the start;
# no test of the run without the feature can get there, and with the feature pruefbau the mutant does not build. The
# function exists only in the test build, so it stays here for good (point 25 of contract start, closed 26.11.2026).
erster re crates/lauf/src/uebergabe.rs:244:5: replace bwrap_halten -> Fehler with Default::default\(\)
